00:01:41.646 --> 00:01:42.479
(bell chimes)

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:43.807
"then congratulations,

00:01:43.807 --> 00:01:45.600
"you might be a femcel."

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.090
So this article got a lot of heat

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:51.510
on TikTok and Twitter
mostly for a lot of reasons.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.360
Me personally, when I read
this article, the first thing

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.890
that came up into my head
was is this not just Tumblr

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.580
sad girl 2014 culture repackaged?

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.980
I mean, "Gone Girl" came out in 2012,

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.160
and I still remember people
making GIFs and graphics

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.560
using that monologue that she says.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.090
- [Amy] Cool girl is hot.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.943
Cool girl is game, cool girl is fun.

00:02:14.943 --> 00:02:17.430
Cool girl never gets angry at her man.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.140
- Lana Del Rey and Marina and the Diamonds

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.770
were the poster girls of
the Tumblr sad girl era,

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.730
and we didn't have "My Year
of Rest and Relaxation",

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.470
but the vibes were the same.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:32.370
So none of this was seriously
shocking to me to read about.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.220
Other people read this and
were understandably upset

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.680
by the categorization of femcel

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.980
and the implication that
listening to Fiona Apple

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.250
would bring you anywhere
close to that identifier.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.360
And for anyone who doesn't know,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.873
the term femcel is short for
female involuntary celibate,

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:53.610
AKA women who cannot
get laid not by choice.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.900
And then there are just
people who are upset

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.430
about being categorized at all

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.050
for having particular interests.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.570
Like just because you read
this one book and you like it,

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.630
or just because you like
this one female artist,

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.400
why do you have to be put and shoved

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.140
into this aesthetic category?

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.390
This TikTokker posted a
video complaining about it

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.227
with the caption, "I'll
never forgive you all

00:03:11.227 --> 00:03:12.577
"for what you've done to Fiona Apple.

00:03:12.577 --> 00:03:14.827
"She's not a femcel, that
is literally not a thing,

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.747
"and she's not a part of this stupid niche

00:03:16.747 --> 00:03:19.177
"'Girl, Interrupted', red
scare, coquette, Lana Del Rey,

00:03:19.177 --> 00:03:21.007
"Diet Coke, Kate Moss shit.

00:03:21.007 --> 00:03:23.017
"Leave her alone and stop
grouping female artists

00:03:23.017 --> 00:03:24.877
"into a box they never agreed to be in.

00:03:24.877 --> 00:03:27.120
"She would those people, and I know it."

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.720
So I understand these
criticisms and complaints,

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.520
but as someone who's perpetually online,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.880
and I mean that in the most
derogatory way possible,

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.730
I understand what Lanigan
was getting on about.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:43.293
Because yes, there is
this growing subcommunity

00:03:43.293 --> 00:03:47.610
on the internet, mostly on
TikTok and Tumblr and Twitter,

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:52.610
who are using femcel as
this aesthetic designator,

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.450
who've become somewhat obsessed
with categorizing themselves

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.090
based on specific niche interests.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.220
It reminds me of the Substack essay

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.100
that my friend Rayne Fisher-Quann
wrote a few months ago.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.687
She writes, "It's become
very common for women online

00:04:07.687 --> 00:04:08.797
"to express their identities

00:04:08.797 --> 00:04:10.297
"through an artfully curated list

00:04:10.297 --> 00:04:12.697
"of the things they consume
or aspire to consume.

00:04:12.697 --> 00:04:14.857
"And because young women
are conditioned to believe

00:04:14.857 --> 00:04:16.177
"that their identities are defined

00:04:16.177 --> 00:04:18.487
"almost entirely by their neuroses,

00:04:18.487 --> 00:04:21.187
"these roundups of cultural
trends and authors du jour

00:04:21.187 --> 00:04:23.377
"often implicitly serve to chicly signal

00:04:23.377 --> 00:04:25.567
"one's mental illnesses to the public.

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:26.857
"One girl on your TikTok feed

00:04:26.857 --> 00:04:29.137
"might be a self-described
Joan Didion/Eve Babitz/

00:04:29.137 --> 00:04:32.257
"Marlboro Red/straight-cut
Levis/fleabag girl.

00:04:32.257 --> 00:04:33.090
"This means

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.567
"she has depression.
(bell chimes)

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.757
"Another will call
herself a babydoll dress/

00:04:36.757 --> 00:04:40.027
"Sylvia Plath/red scare/Miu
Miu/Lana Del Rey girl.

00:04:40.027 --> 00:04:41.227
"Eating disorder.

00:04:41.227 --> 00:04:43.507
"Or a green juice/claw
clip/Emma Chamberlain/

00:04:43.507 --> 00:04:45.367
"yoga mat/podcast girl.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:47.377
"Different eating disorder.

00:04:47.377 --> 00:04:50.077
"The aesthetics of consumption
have in turn become a conduit

00:04:50.077 --> 00:04:52.177
"to make the self more easily consumable,

00:04:52.177 --> 00:04:55.567
"Your existence as a type of
girl has almost nothing to do

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:58.297
"with whether you actually read
Joan Didion or wear Mui Mui,

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:00.877
"and everything to do with
whether you want to be seen

00:05:00.877 --> 00:05:02.670
"as the type of person who would."

